                <pb facs="0637" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg565"/>

                <head>Government of the Canton of Basel Town</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Basel</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-06">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 6, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor and council of the canton of Basel-Stadt to the
                        Bundesrath, in Berne</hi>.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: We learn from the public papers that
                    your supreme authorities have voted an address of sympathy and condolence to the
                    United States, on account of the death of their worthy President, at a time when
                    long-desired peace was just taking the place of a terrible war.</p>
                <p>We presume the address is in the name of all the cantons, and we are thankful for
                    the opportunity of adding our names to it. But if we are mistaken, we suggest
                    that a circular be promulged for the purpose, that each canton may know what to
                    do.</p>
                <p>We commend you to the protection of Divine Providence, and subscribe
                    ourselves,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>C. STCHLIN, <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor</hi>
                            </item>
                            <item>DR. BISCONOFF, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
